{
  "$comment": [
    "SHARED, EXTERNALLY FIXED ROUTING-AAD TEST VECTORS (review 2 §P0.1).",
    "",
    "Read by all three implementations of the canonical routing AAD:",
    "  - protocol/typescript/src/crypto/envelope-crypto.ts    (buildRoutingAad)",
    "  - app/lib/core/protocol/protocol_adapter.dart          (EnvelopeCodec.buildAad)",
    "  - strideterm: electron/backend/mobile/mobile-crypto.ts (hand mirror)",
    "",
    "The AAD is UTF-8 of a JSON object with exactly the keys protocolVersion, pairId,",
    "sourceDeviceId, targetDeviceId, messageId, messageType, sessionKeyVersion, createdAt and expiresAt,",
    "in that order, with no whitespace. These fixtures exist so the ordering and escaping are",
    "pinned by data rather than by three independent readings of a prose rule: a serializer that",
    "reordered keys or escaped non-ASCII differently would look perfectly correct in isolation and",
    "would silently fail every cross-runtime decrypt.",
    "",
    "The fourth case is the recipient-isolation property in fixture form: two events identical in",
    "every field except targetDeviceId must not share an AAD, so a record moved from one phone",
    "mailbox to another's fails the AEAD instead of merely being in the wrong place.",
    "",
    "Regenerate with: node scripts/generate-aad-vectors.mjs"
  ],
